description:
Design a clock divider circuit that takes an input clock signal and produces an output clock signal with a reduced frequency. The module features a programmable division factor specified by the parameter `divval`. On each rising edge of the input clock (`clk_in`), the internal counter increments until it reaches the value of `divval`. Upon reaching this value, the counter resets, and the output clock signal (`clk_out`) toggles, thus outputting a clock signal that is effectively `clk_in` divided by `divval`. The reset functionality ensures the module can be initialized to a known state.
module top_module(
    input clk_in,
	 input reset,
    output reg clk_out
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input clk_in,
	 input reset,
    output reg clk_out
    );parameter divval = 10;

reg[31:0] cntr;


always @( posedge clk_in or negedge reset) begin
	if(reset == 0) begin
		cntr <= 32'd0 ;
		clk_out <= 0;
	end
	else begin
		if(cntr == divval)                             
			begin
			cntr <= 0;
			clk_out <= ~clk_out;
			end
		else
			begin
			cntr <= cntr + 32'd1;
			end
	end
end	



endmodule

