Design a circuit that compares two 32-bit floating-point numbers, `x` and `y`, and outputs a single bit `z` indicating whether `x` is less than `y`. The module extracts the sign, exponent, and mantissa components from the inputs and performs the comparison based on the IEEE 754 floating-point representation rules, handling cases for sign differences and comparing exponents and mantissas accordingly. When `x` is less than `y`, the output `z` is set to 1; otherwise, it is set to 0.
